/*!
\page page_stoftofcollection StTofCollection — Collection Documentation

\section tof_overview Overview

\ref StTofCollection is the event-level container for the <b>legacy STAR
Time-of-Flight (TOF)</b> system — the TOFp and TOFr patch detectors that
preceded the full Barrel TOF (BTOF).  It is <b>superseded by
\ref StBTofCollection</b> for Run 8 (2008) and later data.

The collection stores reconstructed hits (\ref StTofHit), scintillator slats
(\ref StTofSlat), cells (\ref StTofCell), and raw data objects
(\ref StTofData, \ref StTofRawData), together with event-wise pVPD summary
quantities (hit patterns, event start time, vertex z).

\section tof_ownership Object Ownership

All five \c StSPtrVec data members own their elements; elements are deleted when
the vector is destroyed.  The \ref StTofCollection destructor itself is a
<b>no-op</b>; cleanup is delegated to the \c StSPtrVec mechanism and ultimately
to the \c StEvent framework (\c StXRefMain / \c St_DataSet).

\section tof_members Data Members

| Type | Name | Default | Description |
|------|------|---------|-------------|
| \c UInt_t | mVpdEast | 0 | VPD east hit-pattern bitmask (one bit per tube). |
| \c UInt_t | mVpdWest | 0 | VPD west hit-pattern bitmask. |
| \c Float_t | mTstart | −999 | Event start time from the VPD [ns]. |
| \c Float_t | mTdiff | −999 | VPD east–west time difference [ns]. |
| \c Float_t | mVzVpd | −999 | Primary vertex z from the VPD [cm]. |
| \c StSPtrVecTofSlat | mTofSlats | empty | TOFp/TOFr scintillator slats. |
| \c StSPtrVecTofCell | mTofCells | empty | TOF cell objects. |
| \c StSPtrVecTofHit | mTofHits | empty | Reconstructed TOF hits. |
| \c StSPtrVecTofData | mTofData | empty | TOFp raw data objects. |
| \c StSPtrVecTofRawData | mTofRawData | empty | TDC raw data objects (Run 5+). |

\section tof_methods Key Methods

| Method | Description |
|--------|-------------|
| \c vpdEast() / \c vpdWest() | VPD hit-pattern bitmask for east / west side. |
| \c numberOfVpdEast() / \c numberOfVpdWest() | Number of fired VPD tubes (popcount of bitmask). |
| \c tstart() | Event start time from VPD [ns]. |
| \c tdiff() | East–west time difference [ns]. |
| \c vzVpd() | VPD-derived primary vertex z [cm]; −999 if unavailable. |
| \c tofHits() | Mutable reference to reconstructed hit collection. |
| \c tofSlats() / \c tofCells() / \c tofData() / \c tofRawData() | Mutable references to the other sub-collections. |
| \c addHit / \c addSlat / \c addCell / \c addData / \c addRawData | Null-safe append to the corresponding collection. |
| \c hitsPresent() / \c slatsPresent() / \c cellsPresent() / \c dataPresent() / \c rawdataPresent() | Non-empty checks. |

\section tof_example Usage Example

\code{.cpp}
StTofCollection* tofColl = event->tofCollection();
if (!tofColl) return;

int nEast = tofColl->numberOfVpdEast();
int nWest = tofColl->numberOfVpdWest();
float vz  = tofColl->vzVpd();  // -999 if unavailable

if (tofColl->hitsPresent()) {
    const StSPtrVecTofHit& hits = tofColl->tofHits();
    for (size_t i = 0; i < hits.size(); ++i) {
        StTofHit* hit = hits[i];
        // use hit->...
    }
}
\endcode

\note This class is superseded by \ref StBTofCollection for Run 8+ data.

\see StBTofCollection, StTofHit, StTofSlat, StTofCell
*/
